    {
      "type": "pullQuote",
      "content": "Important Articles of the Indian Constitution",
      "id": "yaj1h2o"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Article 14 guarantees Equality before Law and Equal Protection of the Laws within India.",
        "Article 21 provides Protection of Life and Personal Liberty, serving as the bedrock of fundamental rights.",
        "Article 32 grants the Right to Constitutional Remedies, enabling citizens to move the Supreme Court for rights enforcement.",
        "Article 280 mandates the constitution of a Finance Commission every five years for fiscal distribution.",
        "Article 368 empowers Parliament to amend the Constitution and lays down the procedures for amendments."
      ],
      "id": "chlemkb"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "8d1sff8",
      "content": "• Article 32 is called the 'Heart and Soul of the Constitution'."
    },
    {
